('ganja',NULL,'Baku','Baku','77',77,'Day Trip',NULL,NULL,NULL,'08:00 – Leaving Baku to Ganja (1 way x 5.5 hours)  13:00 – Lunch Break  13:35 – Visit Nizami Ganjavi Mausoleum & Museum  - The mausoleum of the great Azerbaijani poet Nizami Ganjavi is one of Ganja’s most important historical landmarks. Restored in 1990–1991, the complex is now a protected heritage site. The lower chambers contain the poet’s crypt, while the surrounding square features sculptures inspired by Nizami’s famous literary work, Khamsa.  - In front of the mausoleum is the Nizami Ganjavi Museum, displaying original and replica manuscripts, rare miniatures, monographs, and books dedicated to the poet. Items exhibited include works preserved in world-renowned libraries and museums across Austria, Germany, Russia, the UK, Egypt, France, and the United States. The museum also includes a conference hall hosting cultural and educational programs.  14:00 – Walk along Javad Khan Street  - One of Ganja’s main pedestrian streets, Javad Khan Street is named after the last khan of Ganja. Known for its historical red-brick architecture, the street blends renovated and original buildings, preserving traditional patterns and ornamentation. It is a lively, scenic location popular with both locals and visitors — ideal for strolling, sightseeing, and photography.   15:00 – Visit Nizami Ganjavi Square & Javad Khan Tomb  - This area holds great cultural and historical importance. The Javad Khan Mausoleum commemorates the bravery of Ganja’s last ruler, who died defending the city. The memorial stands as a meaningful tribute to past struggles and the resilience of the region.   16:00 – Leaving Ganja to Baku (1 way x 5,5 hours)   21:00 – Dinner Break (if included)   22:00 – Drop to the Hotel   Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',77.0),
