('sheki',NULL,'Gabala','Gabala','30',30,'Day Trip',NULL,NULL,NULL,'08:00 – Leaving Gabala to Sheki (1 way x 1.5 hrs)   09:30 – Arrive in Sheki   09:45 – Visit Church of Kish  - Kish is one of the oldest villages in Azerbaijan, famous for its ancient Church of Saint Elisha, dating from the 10th–12th centuries. Scholars believe the church stands on the original site founded by St. Elisha, making it one of the oldest spiritual centers in the Caucasus.   10:45 – Explore Sheki Fortress  - Built to protect the historic city center (now a UNESCO World Heritage Site), the fortress originally had 8-meter-high walls and 2-meter-thick fortifications with defensive towers and arched gateways. Some parts have been restored, allowing visitors to experience its historic significance.   11:45 – Visit Sheki Karavansaray  - This Silk Road caravanserai historically provided safe lodging for merchants traveling with camels and goods. Today, it is one of Sheki’s iconic landmarks and a must-see cultural site.   12:30 – Taste Sheki Halva  - Enjoy Sheki’s famous traditional halva — one of the region’s most beloved culinary specialties.   13:00 – Lunch Break    14:00 – Arrive back in Gabala    18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)    19:00 – Drop to the Hotel   Overnight in Gabala',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',30.0),
