('besbarmaq mountains',NULL,'Baku','Baku','30',30,'Day Trip',NULL,NULL,NULL,'09:00 – Leaving Baku to Beshbarmag (1 way x 1.5 hrs)  10:30 – Arrive at Beshbarmag Mountain   10:45 – Visit Beshbarmag Mountain  • Beshbarmag (literally “Five Fingers Mountain”) stands at about 382 m / ≈ 500 m above sea level and is a famous natural and spiritual landmark near the Caspian Sea.   • The hike/trail from the car park to the rocky peak (or sacred “pir / shrine” zone) is fairly accessible; many visit to enjoy the views of the sea and surrounding plains, or for its local spiritual significance.    12:30 – Leaving Beshbarmag to Baku (1 way x 1,5 hrs)   14:00 – Lunch Break    15:00 – Drop to the Hotel      Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',30.0),
