('sheki-ganja',NULL,'Gabala','Gabala','71',71,'Day Trip',NULL,NULL,NULL,'08:00 – Leaving Gabala to Sheki (1 way x 1.5 hrs)   09:30 – Arrive at Sheki    - Church of Kish – An ancient church dating back to the 10–12th centuries, one of the oldest spiritual centers in the Caucasus.  - Sheki Fortress – Historic fortress with partial restoration, originally built to protect the city center.  - Sheki Karavansaray – A Silk Road inn used by merchants, now a cultural landmark.  - Sheki Halva Tasting – Traditional sweet specialty, highly recommended for visitors.   12:30 - Lunch Break    13:30 – Leaving Sheki to Ganja (1 way x 2.5 hrs)   16:00 – Arrive at Ganja   - Nizami Ganjavi Mausoleum – Honoring Azerbaijan’s famous poet, featuring a beautifully restored monument and crypt.  - Javad Khan Tomb – Memorial to Ganja’s last khan, who defended the city; a historical landmark.  - Javad Khan Street – Central street showcasing Ganja’s architectural heritage and cultural vibe.   18:00 – Leaving Ganja to Gabala   20:30 – Dinner Break (if included)    21:30 – Drop to the hotel  Overnight in Gabala',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',71.0),
