('gobustan + boulevard tour',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','41',41,'Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'09:00 – Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)  10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park  - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.   12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku (1 way x 45 mins)  13:00 – Lunch Break  14:00 – Baku Boulevard tour starts along the Boulevard (Photostop) by followed places:   - Mini Venice of Baku – A charming canal area where you can enjoy gondola-style boat rides in the heart of the city.  - Deniz Mall – A modern seafront shopping and entertainment center with restaurants, cinemas, and family attractions.  - Ferris Wheel – A scenic observation wheel offering beautiful panoramic views of the Caspian Sea and Baku Boulevard.  - Carpet Museum – A uniquely designed museum showcasing Azerbaijan’s rich carpet-weaving heritage and centuries-old masterpieces.  - Crystal Hall – A spectacular indoor arena famous for hosting major concerts and international events.   18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)   19:00 – Drop to the Hotel    Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',41.0),
